Z||000005||1FST2M6||03-19-2001||04:03 PM||||it's a pressure release vent.. at about 85mph my headlight doors would fly up.. on both this car and my SE. after tying 4"ish pieces of yarn to the stainless mesh under 45mph it just scratches the paint..  above 45 it flutters up and down .. at 85+ the yarn is nearly perpandicular to the hood.and the headlamp doors don't open up and cause the car to steer it's self.  <P><BR>oh and only the 1/8th.. cause that all it is.. the 1/4mi. track is over an hour away... so i'll have to settle... till my cars faster.. then i'll make the trek out there.. i did that in the SE a few times.. just cause i knew the 1/8th wasn't the normal track everythings guaged on.<p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 03-19-2001).]||||reg||1
